add([(1817,'statement','Simultaneous colour and depth streams.','premise'),(1827,'statement','Centroid combined with depth for 3D localization.','premise')],'registration','Colour pixel and depth association','Why is simultaneous capture not enough to justify looking up raw depth at the same (u,v) index as an RGB centroid?', [('Different cameras can have different intrinsics and viewpoints, so matching/alignment must be established.','Time association and geometric pixel registration are distinct requirements.'),('A centroid is always expressed in joint angles rather than pixels.','The detected image centroid is an image-space quantity.'),('All RGB pixels necessarily have zero depth.','Valid depth can be associated geometrically, but not merely by assuming identical arrays.'),('Changing the marker ID numerically aligns the two image grids.','Marker identity does not perform colour/depth registration.')],typ='scenario')
