add([(1818,'statement','Unique marker ID from the internal binary pattern.','premise')],'dictionary','Marker ID is not physical identity','Two identical copies of one dictionary marker are visible. What should a localization system recognize about their IDs?', [('They can decode to the same ID; the code identifies a dictionary entry, not a unique printed object.','Duplicating the pattern duplicates its decoded identity unless additional spatial/context logic distinguishes copies.'),('The closer print automatically receives ID 0 and the farther ID 1.','Distance does not renumber dictionary entries.'),('Rotation necessarily gives each copy a new ID.','Marker decoding accounts for orientation rather than changing identity by rotation.'),('The ID numerically equals the marker-to-robot distance in millimetres.','The identifier is not a metric translation.')],typ='scenario',evidence=['aruco'])
